Reason:
The original code only checked that the embedded INIT chunk length did not exceed the remaining cookie payload, but did not enforce a minimum length of `sizeof(struct sctp_init_chunk)`, allowing a truncated INIT header that leads to out-of-bounds reads in `sctp_process_init()`. Additionally, `raw_addr_list_len` was not validated against the remaining cookie space after the INIT chunk, so `sctp_assoc_set_bind_addr_from_cookie()` (which calls `sctp_raw_to_bind_addrs()`) can read beyond the cookie payload when the address list length is oversized.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
chlen = ntohs(ch->length);
if (chlen < sizeof(struct sctp_init_chunk))
    goto malformed;
if (chlen > len - fixed_size)
    goto malformed;
if (bear_cookie->raw_addr_list_len > len - fixed_size - chlen)
    goto malformed;
Reason:
The fix adds three validation steps: (1) ensures the INIT chunk length is at least the size of `struct sctp_init_chunk` to prevent a truncated header; (2) retains the upper bound check; (3) verifies that the raw address list length does not exceed the remaining cookie space after the INIT chunk. These checks together block malformed COOKIE_ECHO chunks from causing out-of-bounds reads.

